    <conditions>party_type=Person</conditions>
    <description>Polymorphic field-rendering UI Policy on x_casemgmt_case_party for the Person branch of the party_type discriminator. Implements the ServiceNow-native equivalent of ArkCase's @DiscriminatorColumn(cm_class_name) single-table inheritance pattern from PersonAssociation.java per AAP Section 0.4.3 ("Polymorphic association via single-table choice + UI Policy"). When party_type=Person the single sys_ui_policy_action child makes the person reference field visible and mandatory; because reverse_if_false=true, any other party_type value - including empty - reverses that action so person becomes hidden and not mandatory. This policy deliberately acts on the person field ONLY: the organization field is owned exclusively by the companion policy "Case Party Conditional Fields - Organization", so the two policies can never contend for the same field and their relative order is irrelevant. Declarative actions plus reverse_if_false give the platform a watched field (party_type, taken from the condition) so the state is re-evaluated on every change, not only at form load; on_load=true additionally applies the correct state when an existing party record is opened. run_scripts is false and both script bodies are empty - there is no imperative logic. cleared=false on the action so toggling party_type never destroys a value the user already entered. The person field is nullable at the dictionary level (../dictionary/x_casemgmt_case_party_person.xml) precisely so that its required-ness can be conditional here.</description>
